{#- Renders nothing until site.newsletter.username is filled in, so the site
    never ships a form that posts into the void.

    The form posts straight to Buttondown rather than going through JavaScript:
    a static site has no server to accept it, and a plain form submission keeps
    working with JS disabled. Buttondown handles the confirmation email, the
    double opt-in and the unsubscribe link, which is what keeps this compliant
    with GDPR and CAN-SPAM without us storing anyone's address. -#}
{% if site.newsletter.username %}
<aside class="subscribe" aria-labelledby="subscribe-heading">
  <div class="subscribe-inner">
    <h2 class="subscribe-title" id="subscribe-heading">{{ site.newsletter.heading }}</h2>
    <p class="subscribe-blurb">{{ site.newsletter.blurb }}</p>

    <form
      class="subscribe-form"
      action="https://buttondown.com/api/emails/embed-subscribe/{{ site.newsletter.username }}"
      method="post"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener"
    >
      <label class="subscribe-label" for="bd-email">Email address</label>
      <div class="subscribe-row">
        <input
          class="subscribe-input"
          type="email"
          name="email"
          id="bd-email"
          autocomplete="email"
          required
          placeholder="you@example.com"
        >
        <button class="subscribe-button" type="submit">Subscribe</button>
      </div>
      <p class="subscribe-fine">
        One email a week, on {{ site.newsletter.sendDay }}. Unsubscribe in one click. No tracking pixels.
      </p>
    </form>
  </div>
</aside>
{% endif %}
